==============================================================================

S = [1, 2, 3, 12, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24, 26, 27, 28, 31]
  P (small) = [1, 2, 3, 12];  L (cluster>13) = [20, 21, 22, 23, 24, 26, 27, 28, 31]
  Vmax = 31;  co-offsets E = Vmax-L = [0, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11]
  NOTE: 0 in E? True  (Vmax itself gives e=0)

  rho*_crit  (maxgap>2/7 cap G_P) = 0 = 0.000000
  rho*_glob  (maxgap>1/7 cap G_P) = 25/42 = 0.595238

  ACTUAL full-S lonely measure L(S) = 0.060654  (# safe arcs = 30)
    widest full-S safe arc: (0.275974,0.282313) width 0.006339, center 0.279143
    witness center is in Vmax-period index k=8 (Vmax*center=8.6534)

  RESOLUTION:
  The criterion-C margin W(S\Vmax)*7*Vmax uses the WIDEST safe arc of
  the OTHER 12 runners over the whole circle. rho*_crit measures the
  MEASURE of P-safe slow-times whose cluster fast-fold leaves a >2/7
  gap.  These differ when the rescuing arc is NOT P-safe-localised in
  the slow variable.  KEY CHECK: is the full-S witness arc P-safe?
    full-S witness center 0.279143: in G_P? True
    cluster maxgap{e_i*center} = 0.279143 (>2/7? False)

==============================================================================
  So rho*_crit=0 means: NO P-safe slow-time has cluster-gap > 2/7.
  But the full-S witness exists because it sits at a slow-time that is
  P-safe with cluster-gap in (1/7, 2/7] -- a GLOBAL witness (gap>1/7),
  not a via-Vmax CRITERION witness (which needs >2/7).  i.e. the
  via-Vmax CRITERION-C-density rho*_crit can be 0 while the GLOBAL
  witness density rho*_glob > 0 carries M(S)>=1/14.
    rho*_glob here = 0.595238 > 0 ? True
==============================================================================

DONE.
